        "subject": "refactor: extract EnqueueCommitStatusGatesForPromotionStrategy helper (#1984)",
        "body": "* refactor: extract EnqueueCommitStatusGatesForPromotionStrategy helper\n\nDeduplicate PromotionStrategy watch enqueue logic across commit-status gate\ncontrollers using field-indexed listing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* refactor: share PromotionStrategy gate enqueue watch handler\n\nExtract EnqueueCommitStatusGatesForPromotionStrategy and\nCommitStatusGatePromotionStrategyWatchHandler so gate controllers\nregister a one-line watch instead of duplicating list-and-enqueue logic.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* refactor: simplify gate list generic and update contributor docs\n\nUse a typed list pointer constraint instead of reflect to allocate\ngate lists, and document CommitStatusGatePromotionStrategyWatchHandler\nfor in-tree gate controllers.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test for list failure\n\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Michael Crenshaw <350466+crenshaw-dev@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>",
